! jb_af1c F216 "MULTIPLY AND ADD TEST", sub-block F216A "ARITHMETIC
! CHECKS", pp.147-148 (octal 020312.00-020367.00, the block's own exit
! "BD,$+1.0").  F216B, the sign and modifier combinations, follows.
!
! THIS BLOCK ADDS *+ (MULTIPLY AND ADD, opcode 0111010), and unlike D*
! and LFT it is not a one-line instruction.  Reference Manual p.98:
! "The operand in the FT register, designated as the multiplicand, is
! multiplied by the operand specified by the effective address,
! designated as the multiplier.  The product is added to the contents
! of the accumulator, bits 0-107."  It is the only operation that READS
! the factor register, which is why F215 had to come first.
!
! In the model it is fpMulDouble feeding fpAddDouble, which is what the
! manual describes: "the intermediate product fraction remains
! unnormalized throughout the addition" and "subsequent to the
! multiplication, an addition is performed similar to that described in
! ADD DOUBLE".
!
! THE ONE PLACE *+ DIFFERS FROM MULTIPLY is the product exponent when
! both multiply operands share a flagged range.  p.99: "When both
! operands are in the XFP range or both in the XFN range, the product
! exponent is the exponent of the operand specified by the EFFECTIVE
! ADDRESS" -- where Figure 32, and so MULTIPLY and D*, give it to the
! accumulator-side operand.  Note this is not a tie-break: it holds
! whatever the two magnitudes are.
!
! HOW EACH SUB-TEST BUILDS A 96-BIT ACCUMULATOR.  DL(U) puts a
! constant's exponent and fraction in IBM 0-59 and zeroes 60-107, then
! C0011(BU,48),FPK27+.12,20 writes FPK27's fraction into IBM 60-107.
! So the accumulator fraction is {constant, FPK27} = {x, 7fffffffffff}.
!
!   A1  acc FK68 +2047 XFP; FT FK59 +1024 XFP; mem FK67 +1791 XFP.
!       Product exponent is the memory operand's +1791; the addition
!       then keeps the accumulator, +2047 being the larger XFP.
!       Result = the accumulator, unchanged.
!   A2  acc FK18 +4 N; FT FK61 -1024 XFN; mem FPK80 +2 N.  XFN
!       dominates N in the product; N beats XFN in the addition, so
!       again the accumulator survives.
!   A3  the same from the other side: FT FPK52 +2 N, mem FK60 -1024 XFN.
!   A4  acc FK18 +4 N; FT FK61 -1024 XFN; mem FK67 +1791 XFP.  XFP
!       dominates in the product and XFP wins the addition, so THE
!       PRODUCT lands in the accumulator -- the first sub-test whose
!       result is not the accumulator it started with.  FK61 x FK67 is
!       29cbb829cbb9 x 800000000000, a clean 47-place shift, so the
!       96-bit product is FK16's fraction over FK67's, which is exactly
!       what the two fraction checks name.
!   A5  acc FK69 -2047 XFN; FT FK59 +1024 XFP; mem FPK80 +2 N.  XFP
!       dominates both times, so the product wins again, at FK59's
!       +1024 -- FK36's exponent field.
!   A6  THE ONLY UNFLAGGED SUB-TEST, and so the only real arithmetic:
!       acc FK18 +4, FT FPK52 +2, mem FPK80 +2.  The product exponent
!       is the SUM, +4, equal to the accumulator's, so nothing shifts
!       and the two 96-bit fractions add directly:
!         eb1a23eb1a23 7fffffffffff  (accumulator)
!       + 14e5dc14e5dc 800000000000  (product)
!       = ffffffffffff ffffffffffff  with no carry out
!       and both halves are checked against FPK32's all-ones fraction.
!
! WHAT F216A CANNOT SEE, worked out before running and then MEASURED.
! A1 is the only sub-test whose multiply operands share a flagged
! range, so it is the only candidate for the memory-wins rule above --
! and it cannot discriminate it either, because the addition discards
! the product whether its exponent is FK67's +1791 or FK59's +1024;
! the accumulator's +2047 beats both.  Injecting Figure 32's tie
! direction in place of p.99's leaves all six sub-tests green, so the
! one rule that makes *+ different from MULTIPLY is untested here.  Nothing here checks an indicator, so
! the LC/LS/PSH/ZM wiring and p.99's generated-vs-propagated rule are
! untouched.  And no sub-test has an exponent difference at all -- A6's
! is zero and the other five never reach the addition's arithmetic --
! so the preparatory shift, the >48 PSH threshold and the >95
! not-added threshold are all untested here.
!
! TRANSCRIPTION NOTE: A5's exponent check is commented "+1026" in the
! scan.  It compares against FK36, whose exponent field is +1024, and
! p.99 gives the product the XFP operand's exponent, FK59's +1024 --
! not the sum 1024+2.  FK36 is also used by F214XA1 as +1024, verified
! there independently.  The comment digit is a misread; the check is
! unambiguous.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes: SERS (octal 1304) -> FAIL halt,
! -- SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch.
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pools pp.176-178) --
        SLC, (8)22040.0
FPK27   DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777677777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22045.0
FPK32   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001177777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22071.0
FPK52   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001024713560247135620
        SLC, (8)22121.0
FPK80   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001100000000000000000
        SLC, (8)22162.0
FK16    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001412345670123456700
        SLC, (8)22164.0
FK18    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0002165432107654321060
        SLC, (8)22206.0
FK36    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1000177777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22235.0
FK59    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1000024713560247135620
FK60    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1000300000000000000000
FK61    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1000224713560247135620
        SLC, (8)22245.0
FK67    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577500000000000000000
FK68    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777565432107654321060
FK69    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777765432107654321060

        SLC, (8)20312.0
! F216A1 - exponents all XFP; the accumulator's +2047 survives
SAP20   DL(U), FK68                          ! exp++2047
        C0011(BU,48), FPK27+.12, 20
        LFT(U), FK59                         ! exp++1024
        *+(U), FK67                          ! exp++1791, adds product to acc.
        CT0110(BU,60), FK68, 68              ! check result exp and high order fract
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK27+.12, 20         ! check low order fract
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
! F216A2 - XFN product against an N accumulator; N wins
        DL(U), FK18                          ! exp++4
        C0011(BU,48), FPK27+.12, 20
        LFT(U), FK61                         ! exp+-1024
        *+(U), FPK80                         ! exp++2
        CT0110(BU,60), FK18, 68              ! check result exp and high order fract
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK27+.12, 20         ! check low order fract
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
! F216A3 - the same with the ranges swapped between FT and memory
        DL(U), FK18                          ! exp++4
        C0011(BU,48), FPK27+.12, 20
        LFT(U), FPK52                        ! exp++2
        *+(U), FK60                          ! exp+-1024
        CT0110(BU,60), FK18, 68              ! check result exp and h o fract
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK27+.12, 20         ! check low order fract
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
! F216A4 - XFP product wins the addition; the product lands in the acc
        DL(U), FK18                          ! exp++4
        C0011(BU,48), FPK27+.12, 20
        LFT(U), FK61                         ! exp+-1024
        *+(U), FK67                          ! exp++1791
        CT0110(BU,12), FK67, 116             ! check result exp++1791
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK16+.12, 68          ! check high order fract
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK67+.12, 20          ! check low order fract
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
! F216A5 - XFP product over an XFN accumulator
        DL(U), FK69                          ! exp+-2047
        C0011(BU,48), FPK27+.12, 20
        LFT(U), FK59                         ! exp++1024
        *+(U), FPK80                         ! exp++2
        CT0110(BU,12), FK36, 116             ! check result exp+ +1024 (see note)
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK16+.12, 68          ! check high order fract
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK67+.12, 20          ! check low order fract
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
! F216A6 - all operands unflagged: the only real 96-bit addition
        DL(U), FK18                          ! exp++4
        C0011(BU,48), FPK27+.12, 20
        LFT(U), FPK52                        ! exp++2
        *+(U), FPK80                         ! exp++2
        CT0110(BU,12), FK18, 116             ! test result exp++4
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK32+.12, 68         ! test high order fract +1-s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK32+.12, 20         ! test low order fract +1-s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                               ! 020367.00: the block's exit "BD,$+1.0"
        END, SAP20
